From: (xbox360 netboot session)
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] powerpc/xenon: enable VMX for kernel context switching, don't advertise AltiVec

Free60 leaves AltiVec off on Xenon, so any vector instruction traps
(vector-unavailable, 0xf20) and the process gets SIGILL: Debian's libLLVM,
built with AltiVec, dies on load.

Enable VMX in the CPU features (CPU_FTR_ALTIVEC_COMP) so code built with
AltiVec runs, but keep AltiVec out of the user-visible features (AT_HWCAP)
and out of /proc/cpuinfo. VMX128 lacks parts of AltiVec (the integer
multiply and sum family): libraries that choose AltiVec at run time
(libjpeg-turbo reads /proc/cpuinfo, pixman, glibc) must keep their scalar
paths, or they die with SIGILL on the missing instructions.

An earlier version of this patch advertised AltiVec and did exactly that
(NetSurf died on the first JPEG; pixman needed PIXMAN_DISABLE=vmx).

---
--- a/arch/powerpc/include/asm/cputable.h	2026-10-29 03:38:23.833342771 -0700
+++ b/arch/powerpc/include/asm/cputable.h	2026-10-29 03:38:23.822126308 -0700
@@ -464,7 +464,7 @@
 	    CPU_FTR_UNALIGNED_LD_STD | CPU_FTR_DABRX)
 #define CPU_FTRS_XENON (CPU_FTR_LWSYNC | \
 	    CPU_FTR_PPCAS_ARCH_V2 | CPU_FTR_CTRL | \
-	    CPU_FTR_MMCRA | CPU_FTR_SMT | \
+	    CPU_FTR_ALTIVEC_COMP | CPU_FTR_MMCRA | CPU_FTR_SMT | \
 	    CPU_FTR_CELL_TB_BUG )
 #define CPU_FTRS_PA6T (CPU_FTR_LWSYNC | \
 	    CPU_FTR_PPCAS_ARCH_V2 | CPU_FTR_ALTIVEC_COMP | \
--- a/arch/powerpc/kernel/cpu_specs_book3s_64.h	2026-10-29 03:38:23.834180659 -0700
+++ b/arch/powerpc/kernel/cpu_specs_book3s_64.h	2026-10-29 03:38:23.824267232 -0700
@@ -504,6 +504,10 @@
 		.pvr_value        = 0x00710000,
 		.cpu_name        = "Xenon",
 		.cpu_features        = CPU_FTRS_XENON,
+		/* VMX is enabled (CPU_FTR_ALTIVEC_COMP: no vector-unavailable SIGILL for
+		 * code built with AltiVec), but not advertised: VMX128 lacks parts of
+		 * AltiVec, and libraries that choose AltiVec at run time (libjpeg-turbo,
+		 * pixman) then die on the missing instructions */
 		.cpu_user_features    = COMMON_USER_PPC64 | PPC_FEATURE_SMT,
 		.mmu_features        = MMU_FTRS_XENON,
 		.icache_bsize        = 128,
--- a/arch/powerpc/kernel/setup-common.c	2026-10-29 03:38:23.834249139 -0700
+++ b/arch/powerpc/kernel/setup-common.c	2026-10-29 03:38:23.825932942 -0700
@@ -242,7 +242,10 @@
 	else
 		seq_printf(m, "unknown (%08x)", pvr);
 
-	if (cpu_has_feature(CPU_FTR_ALTIVEC))
+	/* only when user space is told (Xenon enables VMX without advertising it,
+	 * and libjpeg-turbo reads this line to pick its AltiVec code) */
+	if (cpu_has_feature(CPU_FTR_ALTIVEC) &&
+	    (cur_cpu_spec->cpu_user_features & PPC_FEATURE_HAS_ALTIVEC))
 		seq_puts(m, ", altivec supported");
 
 	seq_putc(m, '\n');
